{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow\/Style"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow\/Style\/other","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarrow\/style\/other"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"other"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLArrowV5StyleO5otheryA2EmF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"other"}],"symbolKind":"case","title":"MXLArrow.Style.other","roleHeading":"Case","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"An arrow style other than those listed here.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArrow/Style/other":{"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLArrow.Style.other","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarrow\/style\/other","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arrow style other than those listed here."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"other"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow\/Style\/other"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArrow/Style":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The arrow-style type represents the style of an arrow, using Unicode arrow terminology. Filled and hollow","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrows indicate polygonal single arrows. Paired arrows are duplicate single arrows in the same direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Combined arrows apply to double direction arrows like left right, indicating that an arrow in one direction","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"should be combined with an arrow in the other direction.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow\/Style","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarrow\/style","title":"MXLArrow.Style","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArrow":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArrow"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrow element represents an arrow used for a musical technical indication. It can represent both Unicode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and SMuFL arrows. The presence of an arrowhead element indicates that only the arrowhead is displayed, not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrow stem. The smufl attribute distinguishes different SMuFL glyphs that have an arrow appearance such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrowBlackUp, guitarStrumUp, or handbellsSwingUp. The specified glyph should match the descriptive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLArrow","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarrow","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArrow"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"}}}